{"n":8,"at":"2026-11-11T19:30:00Z","by":"prima-kernel-seed","op":"put","addr":"10.11.21.1001.01","tail":"draft","body":"## bob\ntype: brand\nbrand: bob.001\nforms: Bob\nmeans: the user's name\n\n## cats\ntype: brand\nbrand: cats.001\nforms: cats\nmeans: animals the user likes","proposal":"prima-kernel-seed:10.11.21.1001"}
{"n":9,"at":"2026-11-11T19:30:00Z","by":"prima-kernel-seed","op":"put","addr":"10.11.21.1001.04","tail":"draft","body":"## bob\nsource: [01 / bob]; Bob test session 1, the user's words: \"My name is Bob and I like cats\"; why from docs/spec/brands.md:7\nwhy: When a user explains their meaning of a word, it is recorded, so models look it up instead of guessing.\n\nSession 1, the user said: \"My name is Bob and I like cats\". Bob is the user's name. Session 2, \"what is my name\", is answered from this card through the dictionary entry `bob` (10.11.21.0012.03.14).\n\n## cats\nsource: [01 / cats]; Bob test session 1, the user's words: \"My name is Bob and I like cats\"; why from docs/spec/brands.md:7\nwhy: When a user explains their meaning of a word, it is recorded, so models look it up instead of guessing.\n\nSession 1, the user said: \"My name is Bob and I like cats\". Bob likes cats.","proposal":"prima-kernel-seed:10.11.21.1001"}
